values ('draft-bridge-g6-batch1-math-expressions-machine', 'bridge', '6', 'math', 'Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions', 'Write, evaluate, and explain expressions with variables by connecting a situation to a repeatable rule.', 'Expressions, Equations, And Variables', '["ccss-math-6-ee"]'::jsonb, 'How does a variable help us describe a pattern before we know every number?', 'This Bridge Academy mission teaches you to use a input-output machine and expression builder before writing a final answer.', 'This is built like a real middle-school class session: the app teaches, you use a visual model, your team builds evidence, the tutor helps with the stuck point, and mastery depends on explanation plus recall.', '["variable","expression","coefficient","operation","substitute"]'::jsonb, '["Can write one complete explanation sentence.","Can point to a model or source before answering.","Can revise after feedback."]'::jsonb, '{"warmUp":"The app shows a cyber-neon input-output machine and expression builder. Write one thing you notice and one question before the rule appears.","directInstruction":"The app teaches expressions, equations, and variables in three beats: concrete situation, visual model, then academic language. The student must explain the model before practice unlocks.","guidedPractice":"Work through one example with feedback. The app asks which part of the input-output machine and expression builder proves each move.","interactiveActivity":"Build or annotate a input-output machine and expression builder. Drag labels, choose evidence, and write one because sentence that connects the model to the answer.","independentPractice":"Complete two solo checks: one familiar problem and one changed-context transfer problem.","reteachPath":"If the learner misses mastery, the app returns to the input-output machine and expression builder, hides extra steps, and asks one first-principles question.","challengePath":"If mastery is strong, the learner creates a new example, predicts a mistake, and writes a tutor hint for another student."}'::jsonb, '[{"title":"Model before answer","note":"Do not score the final answer until the learner connects it to the input-output machine and expression builder."},{"title":"Diagnose the stuck point","note":"Ask whether the learner is stuck on vocabulary, the first step, choosing evidence, or explaining why."},{"title":"Team plus individual proof","note":"The group artifact is shared, but every learner submits one independent evidence sentence."},{"title":"Recall unlock","note":"Reward XP is strongest after the learner can retrieve the idea later, not only during the first attempt."}]'::jsonb, '[{"misunderstanding":"The student treats a variable as a label instead of a value that can change.","repair":"Test the expression with two inputs and explain what stays the same and what changes.","signal":"The response looks complete but does not explain the model-to-answer connection."},{"misunderstanding":"The student copies a vocabulary word without using it in context.","repair":"Ask for a plain-language definition, a visual pointer, and one example from the task.","signal":"The answer contains the word but no evidence or example."},{"misunderstanding":"The student waits for the tutor to give the answer.","repair":"The tutor asks for the first step, shows one hint, and requires a retry before revealing more.","signal":"The student asks for the final answer or says only ''I don''t know.''"}]'::jsonb, '[{"placement":"lesson-hero","title":"Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions mission board","description":"A bold Grade 6 class mission board for Expressions, Equations, And Variables.","prompt":"Create a cyber-neon Grade 6 math lesson hero for Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions. Show input-output machine and expression builder, student mission, and mastery reward. No real children, no private data, no logos.","altText":"Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions mission board with input-output machine and expression builder."},{"placement":"teaching-diagram","title":"input-output machine and expression builder teaching diagram","description":"A labeled diagram that breaks the lesson model into visible parts and one learner action.","prompt":"Create a readable teaching diagram for Grade 6 math: input-output machine and expression builder. Include labels, arrows, one example, and learner action. High contrast, classroom safe.","altText":"input-output machine and expression builder teaching diagram for Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions."},{"placement":"ai-tutor","title":"Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions tutor stuck-point card","description":"Tutor card with stuck-point lanes: vocabulary, first step, visual model, evidence, and explanation.","prompt":"Create a tutor help card for Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions. Show stuck-point lanes and hint-before-answer flow. No real children, no logos.","altText":"Tutor stuck-point card for Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions."},{"placement":"misconception-repair","title":"Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions repair board","description":"Test the expression with two inputs and explain what stays the same and what changes.","prompt":"Create a misconception repair board for Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions. Show wrong idea, model check, repair move, retry. High contrast, short labels.","altText":"Misconception repair board for Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions."},{"placement":"group-homework","title":"Rule Builder Team visual","description":"Create a variable machine for a real classroom pattern and test it with three inputs.","prompt":"Create a group mission board for Rule Builder Team. Include roles, shared artifact, individual proof, and review checklist. Cyber-neon academy style.","altText":"Rule Builder Team group mission visual."}]'::jsonb, '[{"questionText":"What makes an answer strong in Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions?","questionType":"multiple-choice","choices":["It is short","It uses a model and explains the evidence","It copies a vocabulary word","It skips the first step"],"correctAnswer":"It uses a model and explains the evidence","explanation":"Bridge Academy mastery requires evidence and reasoning, not just a final answer.","difficultyLevel":"core","skillTag":"math-expressions-equations-and-variables","standardTag":"ccss-math-6-ee"},{"questionText":"Which move best repairs this misconception: The student treats a variable as a label instead of a value that can change.","questionType":"multiple-choice","choices":["Test the expression with two inputs and explain what stays the same and what changes.","Ask for the final answer","Add more unrelated facts","Skip the visual model"],"correctAnswer":"Test the expression with two inputs and explain what stays the same and what changes.","explanation":"The repair targets the actual misunderstanding and returns to the model.","difficultyLevel":"developing","skillTag":"math-expressions-equations-and-variables-misconception","standardTag":"ccss-math-6-ee"},{"questionText":"What should the tutor ask before giving help?","questionType":"multiple-choice","choices":["What exactly feels confusing?","Do you want me to finish it?","Should we skip the model?","Which reward do you want?"],"correctAnswer":"What exactly feels confusing?","explanation":"The tutor has to diagnose the stuck point before choosing an explanation mode.","difficultyLevel":"core","skillTag":"tutor-confusion-diagnosis","standardTag":"ccss-math-6-ee"},{"questionText":"Why does the group task still require individual evidence?","questionType":"multiple-choice","choices":["So one person can do all the work","So each learner proves their own understanding","So the task is longer","So the quiz can be skipped"],"correctAnswer":"So each learner proves their own understanding","explanation":"Collaboration helps learning, but mastery still needs individual proof.","difficultyLevel":"transfer","skillTag":"math-expressions-equations-and-variables-group-accountability","standardTag":"ccss-math-6-ee"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"bridge-g6-batch1-math","title":"Bridge Academy Batch 1 Grade 6 Mathematics","url":"","claim":"Variable Machine: Build And Test Expressions is an original Nexus lesson aligned to the documented Grade 6 Batch 1 scope and standards tags.","checkedAt":"2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z","reviewerNote":"Original lesson design. External IXL references may guide coverage only and must not be copied."},{"sourceId":"grade-6-california-scope-sequence","title":"Bridge Academy Grade 6 California Scope Sequence","url":"docs/curriculum/grade-6-california-scope-sequence.md","claim":"Batch 1 should cover ratios/rates, expressions/equations, weather systems, close reading/evidence, and early-human historical thinking.","checkedAt":"2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z","reviewerNote":"Local source-of-truth scope sequence for the first sellable Bridge Academy wedge."}]'::jsonb, '{"title":"Rule Builder Team","roles":["Facilitator","Model builder","Evidence checker","Reporter"],"sharedArtifact":"Create a variable machine for a real classroom pattern and test it with three inputs.","individualAccountability":"Each learner explains one part in their own words."}'::jsonb, 'review', '', 'Bridge Academy Batch 1 lesson 2 of 5. Original Nexus content; do not copy proprietary IXL explanations, question banks, or sequence.', 'Every diagram needs alt text, readable labels, keyboard-completable interactions, captions, and a non-color-only explanation path.', 'Grade 6 Bridge Academy pacing: independent but scaffolded, visual first, group artifact with individual accountability, tutor hints before answers.', true, 'ready', '[]'::jsonb, null, '', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 4, '["Truth-policy and standards review required before publication."]'::jsonb, false, 'needs-human-review', '{}'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 0, '2026-07-10T12:00:00.000Z', '2026-07-10T12:00:00.000Z')
